This is the fix for oss-fuzz 29792, which is a 1-byte buffer read-overrun in `arith_uncompress_to`. But our issue is 42491972. Let me check whether 42491972 is the same bug or a different one. 

The issue 42491972 was reported Jan 21, 2021, and the crash state is `arith_uncompress_to -> cram_uncompress_block -> cram_read_SAM_hdr`. The fix commit `a01a139a` (Jan 22, 2021) fixes "1-byte buffer overruns in arith_uncompress_to()". This is very likely the fix for our issue.

The specific fix `cf8eca1` adds a bounds check after `var_get_u32(in+c_meta_len, in_end, &ulen)`:
```c
c_meta_len += var_get_u32(in+c_meta_len, in_end, &ulen);
if (c_meta_len >= in_size)
    return NULL;
unsigned int N = in[c_meta_len++];
```

So the bug is: in the STRIPE mode of `arith_uncompress_to`, after reading the ulen varint, `c_meta_len` could be >= in_size, and then `in[c_meta_len]` reads out of bounds (1-byte read overrun).

Let me look at the current code in the repo to confirm this is the vulnerable code.

